{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLMpwYBsB35QMG4hEZVm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`bug.apart(t)` now returns `-a*t + a/2 - a/(2*(2*t - 1))`, which matches what `apart` gives when `a` is replaced by 1. Before, it returned `-a*t`.\n\nThe cause wasn't in `apart` itself. `Poly.div` computes in the field `ZZ(a)` and then converts the result back to the ring `ZZ[a]`. In `from_FractionField` (`sympy/polys/domains/polynomialring.py`), a ground denominator such as 2 was divided out with truncating integer division. That turned `a*t - a/2` into `a*t` and the remainder `a/2` into 0. The conversion now divides exactly. If the division isn't exact, it fails to convert, and `Poly.div` keeps the result in the field.\n\nThe fix is one line plus the `ExactQuotientFailed` import. I didn't add a regression test, since the rules say not to touch test files.\n\nI ran the partfrac, polytools, polyclasses, rings, constructor and domains tests. Four fail, and none are caused by the fix. `test_noncommutative_pseudomultivariate` in `test_partfrac.py` fails with and without my change. In `test_polytools.py`, `test_factor_noeval`, `test_poly_matching_consistency` and `test_issue_5786` fail without my change too, which I checked on a stash. I didn't check whether the remaining failure from the combined run is the same `test_noncommutative_pseudomultivariate` or `test_factor_noeval`. I also didn't run the full `sympy/polys` suite, which timed out in the foreground."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":278,"cache_read_input_tokens":33253,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":278},"output_tokens":534,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"